        "original_id": "dc32da91-6f07-5464-bddf-44e9af9a9567",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hans Loewald, Martin Heidegger\n- Roles: physician, musician, philosopher\n- Places: Germany, Rome University\n- Concepts: language theory, Continental tradition, philosophical hermeneutics\n\nFacts:\n- Hans Loewald's father died shortly after Hans Loewald's birth and was a Jewish physician interested in dermatology and psychiatry.\n- Hans Loewald's mother was a gifted musician who played the piano.\n- Martin Heidegger was born on 26 September 1889 and died on 26 May 1976.\n- Hans Loewald completed medical training in Germany and also studied philosophy there with Martin Heidegger.\n- Hans Loewald received a medical degree from Rome University in 1935.\n- Martin Heidegger was a German philosopher and a seminal thinker in the Continental tradition and philosophical hermeneutics.\n- Martin Heidegger influenced Hans Loewald through his theory of language.",
